<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="468"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" width="274"> <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/national/03POLL.html"><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" size="+1"><strong>In Poll, Americans Say Both Parties Lack Clear Vision</strong></font></a><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1">By ADAM NAGOURNEY and JANET ELDER</font><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000">The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll found an emerging divide between Democrats and Republicans in their perception of the state of the nation.</font><br> • <font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1"><a href="javascript:pop_me_up2('/imagepages/2002/11/03/national/20021103_POLL2_GRAPHIC.html','440697','width=440,height=697,scrollbars=yes,toolbars=no,resizable=yes');">Graphic: Perceptions of the Parties</a></font><br> • <font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1"><a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/politics/campaigns/03SENA.html">Fight for Senate Grows Feverish</a></font><br> • <font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1"><a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/pages/politics/campaign/index.html">Complete Coverage: The Campaign</a></font><br><br>  <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/aponline/international/AP-Israel-Politics.html"><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" size="+1"><strong>Netanyahu to Accept Israeli Post if Early Elections Are Held</strong></font></a><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1">By THE ASSOCIATED PRESS</font><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000">Benjamin Netanyahu, the hawkish former prime minister of Israel, today announced his condition for taking the foreign minister post in a narrow right-wing government.</font><br><br>  <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/international/asia/03KORE.html"><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" size="+1"><strong>North Korea Says Nuclear Program Can Be Negotiated</strong></font></a><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1">By PHILIP SHENON</font><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000">North Korea says it is open to meeting the Bush administration's demand that it shut down its previously secret uranium-enrichment facilities.</font><br><br>  <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/reuters/international/international-russia-chechnya.html"><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" size="+1"><strong>Russia Launches Military Action in Chechnya; Rebels Hit Chopper</strong></font></a><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1">By REUTERS</font><br><font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000">After Russia announced today that its forces were launching new military action in Chechnya, a Russian helicopter was reported shot down, killing nine.</font><br><br></td><td width="5"><img src="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938im_/http://graphics7.nytimes.com/images/misc/spacer.gif" width="5" height="1" border="0"/></td><td width="1" bgcolor="#999999"><img src="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938im_/http://graphics7.nytimes.com/images/misc/spacer.gif" width="1" height="1" border="0"/></td><td width="5"><img src="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938im_/http://graphics7.nytimes.com/images/misc/spacer.gif" width="5" height="1" border="0"/></td><td align="left" valign="top" width="182"> <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/sports/othersports/03WIRE-MARA.html"><img src="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938im_/http://graphics7.nytimes.com/images/2002/11/03/international/US-NYC-MARATHON-MENS.jpg" width="184" height="171" border="0" align="left" alt="Kenyans Sweep New York Marathon"/></a><br clear="all"><div align="right"><font size="-2">Agence France-Presse</font></div><font size="-1"><strong>A Kenyan Sweep</strong><br>Two Kenyans, Rodgers Rop, above, and Joyce Chepchumba, won the men's and women's races today at the New York City Marathon.</font> &nbsp;<font face="Times New Roman,Times,Serif" color="#000000" size="-1"><a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/sports/othersports/03WIRE-MARA.html">Go to Article</a></font><br><br><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938/http://www.nytimes.com/pages/nyregion/index.html"><font color="#990000" size="-1"><strong>NEW YORK REGION</strong></font></a><br> <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/nyregion/03OLYM.html"><strong>New York City Is U.S. Nominee for '12 Games</strong></a><br><br><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938/http://www.nytimes.com/pages/world/index.html"><font color="#990000" size="-1"><strong>INTERNATIONAL</strong></font></a><br> <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/international/europe/03TURK.html"><strong>As Turkey Votes Today, Religious Issue Prominent</strong></a><br><br><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938/http://www.nytimes.com/pages/national/index.html"><font color="#990000" size="-1"><strong>NATIONAL</strong></font></a><br> <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/2002/11/03/national/03SHOO.html"><strong>The Mentor and the Disciple: How Sniper Suspects Bonded</strong></a><br><br><p>
