<nyt_headline>
<a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/20021103.html"><font size="3" face="times"><b>On Nov. 3 ...<br></b></font></a>
</nyt_headline>
<nyt_byline>
<font size="-1"></font>
</nyt_byline>
<nyt_summary>
<font size="-1">
<b>1936:</b> President Roosevelt was re-elected in a landslide over Republican Alfred M. "Alf" Landon. (<a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/big/1103.html">See this front page. </a> | <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20021103115938/https://query.nytimes.com/nytstore/digivault.html?inpdate=11/04/1936">Buy this front page.</a>)<br>
<b>1903:</b> Walker Evans, the photographer best known for his portrayal of America during the Great Depression, was born.  <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/bday/1103.html">(Read about his life.)</a> <br>
<b>1866:</b> Harper's Weekly featured a cartoon about President Andrew Johnson's controversial "swing around the circle" campaign tour.  <a href="/web/20021103115938/http://graphics.nytimes.com/learning/general/onthisday/harp/1103.html">(See the cartoon.)</a></font>
</td></tr>
